virglrenderer: textureGrad() on shadow array and cube samplers needs no extension

What: TXD (textureGrad/textureGradOffset) on SHADOW2D_ARRAY, SHADOWCUBE and
SHADOWCUBE_ARRAY asked for GL_EXT_texture_shadow_lod, because the gradients sit
in the bias buffer. textureGrad() on these samplers is core GLSL 1.30; the
extension is only needed for the lod/bias forms. The GLES-only rule below is
unchanged.
Why: the Mac has no EXT_texture_shadow_lod and refused the shader, which stopped
the guest context (dEQP-GLES3.functional.shaders.texture_functions.texturegradoffset.*).
Upstreamable; not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-core-glsl-shaders.c "textureGradOffset on a shadow array
sampler", "textureGrad on a shadow cube sampler" (fail without this patch).
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
@@ -3375,8 +3375,10 @@ static void translate_tex(struct dump_ctx *ctx,
 
    bool has_bias = strbuf_get_len (&bias_buf) != 0;
    bool has_offset = strbuf_get_len (&offset_buf) != 0;
-   // EXT_texture_shadow_lod defines a few more functions handling bias
-   if (has_bias &&
+   // EXT_texture_shadow_lod defines a few more functions handling bias.
+   // For TXD bias_buf holds the gradients: textureGrad() on these samplers
+   // is core GLSL 1.30 and needs no extension.
+   if (has_bias && inst->Instruction.Opcode != TGSI_OPCODE_TXD &&
        (inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOW2D_ARRAY ||
         inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE ||
         inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE_ARRAY))
